# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF throughout. Without this file the result depends on
# each contributor's core.autocrlf setting, and on Windows that produces CRLF
# in the working copy. Two files break under CRLF: scripts/setup.sh, which bash
# refuses with "\r: command not found", and the Dockerfile, where a trailing
# carriage return ends up inside RUN commands.

# Default: normalise to LF in the repository, leave the working copy to the
# platform for text files where it does not matter.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must be LF wherever they are checked out.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.mako          text eol=lf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.zip           binary
